<section id="top">
        <div class="page-shell about-page-intro">
            <span class="eyebrow">United Arab Emirates</span>
            <h1>No-App Site Inspections for UAE Field Teams</h1>
            <p class="page-lede">Your supervisors are already on WhatsApp all day. Quickler turns that into the inspection tool. A field team walking a site, checking plant and equipment, or running a vehicle check answers a few prompts on the phone in their pocket. No app to install. No tablet to issue, charge or replace. Each check lands as a structured digital record on a manager dashboard, with a PDF you can export the moment a client or contractor asks for one.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="content-duo">
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">The scenario</p>
                        <h2>A morning site walk, three trades, one phone each</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Picture a typical UAE contract: a site supervisor opening up, a plant operator checking the excavator and the generator, and a driver running a pre-shift vehicle check on the crew van. On paper, that is three clipboards that end the day creased in a glovebox. On a tablet app, it is three devices to provision, log into and keep charged in 45-degree heat.</p>
                    <p>With Quickler, each person opens WhatsApp and works through the prompts:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>The supervisor confirms access, edge protection and housekeeping, snapping a photo where something is wrong.</li>
                        <li>The plant operator records fluid levels, guards and warning lights, sending a voice note for the detail.</li>
                        <li>The driver logs tyres, lights, brakes and load security before the van leaves the yard.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Nobody downloads anything. Nobody is handed a new device. The work happens on the tool everyone already carries.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">What the manager sees</p>
                        <h2>A live record, not a pile of paper</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>As answers come in, they build a clean, structured digital record on the manager dashboard. Each item carries a red, amber or green status, so a cracked guard or a bald tyre is visible the instant it is reported rather than at the end of the week when the paper finally surfaces.</p>
                    <p>That means the office can act while the team is still on site: send a part, hold a vehicle off the road, or escalate a hazard before it becomes an incident.</p>
                    <p>When a document is needed for a client, a principal contractor or an authority, you export a tidy PDF from the same record in one step. The structured record is the asset; the PDF is the convenience copy.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="content-duo">
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">Why no app matters here</p>
                        <h2>Less friction on multi-trade, multi-site contracts</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>UAE field work mixes permanent staff, subcontractors and short-term crews. Getting a tablet app onto every one of those phones is a real cost: provisioning, training, locked-down devices, and the device that is always flat or left in another van.</p>
                    <p>Removing the app removes that whole layer. A new subcontractor on site this morning can complete their first check before lunch, because the instruction is simply a WhatsApp number. When the contract ends, there is nothing to recover and no licence to claw back.</p>
                    <p>It is also one less per-user fee. Quickler does not charge by the head, so adding the next crew does not add to the bill.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">Your forms, your rules</p>
                        <h2>Any inspection, not a fixed template</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Quickler is job-agnostic. It is not tied to one type of certificate. Upload the inspection or checklist form you already use and Quickler builds it into a WhatsApp workflow that follows your wording, your sections and your pass and fail logic.</p>
                    <p>That covers the spread of real UAE field work: site safety walks, scaffold and access checks, plant and lifting equipment, fire safety rounds, HVAC and plumbing service records, facilities checks, and fleet and vehicle inspections.</p>
                    <p>The roots are in UK compliance, where checks like the EICR electrical report and the CP12 gas certificate were the first workflows. The engine underneath is the same one that runs your own forms, wherever the site is.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">Common questions</p>
                <h2>No-app inspections in the UAE</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-3">
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Do field workers need to install anything?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">No. Quickler runs inside WhatsApp, which your team already has. They answer by text, voice note or photo. No app store download, no tablet to issue or charge on site.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">What does a check produce?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">A structured digital record on a manager dashboard, with red, amber and green status on every item. Export a PDF from that record whenever a client or authority needs a document.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Can we use our own UAE forms?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Yes. Upload your site safety walk, equipment check, scaffold inspection or vehicle check, and Quickler builds it into a WhatsApp workflow that follows your wording and your rules.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Where is the data held?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">On EU servers in Germany, GDPR-aligned. Workflows run in English today, with more languages on the roadmap. See <a href="/pages/global-field-compliance.html">field compliance that works anywhere</a> and our <a href="/pages/services.html">workflows</a>.</p>
            </article>
